TEXT -600 -128 Left 4 ;sign corrected model mvz=-1\nnetoperation mode
TEXT -912 -128 Left 4 ;my historical model mvz=1(default)\nnetoperation mode
TEXT -288 -184 Left 4 ;NOTE: \nLTspice uses the load reference arrow system.\nTherefore active power P has negative sign\nif the machine acts as generator.\nTo fullfill the Equation P=M*omega\nM has to be negative for positive omega \nwhich means (clockwise rotation).\nFor my models for historical reason and \nto be compatible with my old examples \nM was positive for clockwise rotation.\nIf you want to go with the correct sign convention set mvz=-1\nfor the generator model and negate\nthe output of the speed controller (if present) \nas in the example below\nBecause of a bug in the excitation system (factor 2/3) \nfor new examples dont't use the old DSG and Block1 \nsynchronous machine models
TEXT -816 408 Left 2 ;round rotor gen
TEXT -944 504 Left 4 ;M=neg n=pos P=neg
TEXT -920 520 Left 2 ;P=M*omega sign OK!\nomega=2*pi*n/60
TEXT -936 256 Left 4 ;sign corrected model mvz=-1\nisolated mode (positive omega)
TEXT -784 456 Left 2 ;For Mvz=-1
TEXT -960 552 Left 2 ;controlled PI-Regler ( KP-TN-Controll )
TEXT -960 560 Left 2 !vpwl  nsoll 0 pwl 0s 1500 \nvkp Kp 0 pwl 0s 200000 6s 60000\nvtn Tn 0 pwl 0s 0.01  6s 0.05\nvlimUp LimUp 0 pwl 0s 3000000\nvlimLo LimLo 0 pwl 0s 0\nven2 en2 0 1
TEXT -496 408 Left 2 ;round rotor gen
TEXT -624 504 Left 4 ;M=neg n=pos P=neg
TEXT -600 520 Left 2 ;P=M*omega sign OK!\nomega=2*pi*n/60
